# Skill: MCP Runtime Operations

Purpose:
  Engineering skill for operating MCP (Model Context Protocol) integrations
  safely — activation, hash pinning, output DLP, sandboxing. Use when
  connecting external tool servers to the SDDRA runtime.

Owns: engineering/mcp-runtime-ops.sdd

Source: research round 3 r4 (2026-09-07) — OWASP MCP Top 10, NSA-CISA MCP
  Security Design Considerations, invariant-labs mcp-scan, Docker MCP
  Catalog; sources cited in .sdd/runtime/mcp-allowlist.sdd.

Patterns:
  allowlist_governance:
    - only allowlisted servers connect; activation is human-gated,
      append-only record
  hash_pinning:
    - SHA-256 tool schemas captured at activation; re-verified every
      session start; changed definition => BLOCK until re-approval
      (rug-pull defense, CVE-2025-54136)
  tier_discipline:
    - 6-server core (github, filesystem, git, context7, playwright +
      chrome-devtools default), "six not fifty"; tool-count degradation
  output_dlp:
    - multi-pass scan (normalized text, invisible Unicode, base64/hex)
      on every tool output before memory entry — parameter names,
      defaults, enums, error messages are all injection surfaces
  sandboxing:
    - Docker-only, non-root, read-only root fs, bind-mounted dirs,
      DNS egress allowlists (DuneSlide-class escape defense)
  spec_targeting:
    - 2026-07-28 spec: stateless core, server/discover, cacheable
      tools/list, OAuth 2.1 + CIMD; never build on deprecated
      Roots/Sampling/Logging
  threat_model:
    - tool poisoning (desc injection), line jumping (handshake
      poisoning), rug pull (post-approval change), cross-server
      shadowing, squatting, sandbox escape, zero-click config hijack

AntiPatterns:
  - @latest versions; unknown-publisher servers; vision-class browsing
    where DOM works; trusting archived reference servers

Rules:
  [MRO1] Apply via .sdd/runtime/mcp-allowlist.sdd + mcp-integration.sdd —
         specs are authority.
  [MRO2] MCP operations cite pattern provenance.

